| Purpose | JSON Schema words |
| --- | --- |
| Kind of value | `type` (string, number, integer, boolean, object, array, null) |
| Shape of an object | `properties`, `required`, `additionalProperties` (true or false) |
| Shape of a list | `items`, `minItems`, `maxItems` |
| Allowed values | `enum`, `const` |
| Size | `minLength`, `maxLength`, `minimum`, `maximum` |
| Reuse | `$ref` and `$defs`, within the project only |
| Notes for people and agents | `title`, `description` |

- **References within the project are supported from the start**, so one relic type can be composed from pieces of another. [Decided]
- A schema can reuse a definition from inside itself, or from another relic type in the same project. [Proposed]
- A reference to another type is fixed to that type's version at the moment the schema is saved. A saved schema version therefore never changes meaning when the other type moves on. [Proposed]
- References to web addresses, to anything outside the project, or in a loop are refused when the schema is saved. [Proposed]

Left out at first: pattern matching, format checks, and combining schemas with `allOf`, `anyOf`, `oneOf` or `not`.
